  "description": "As KS-49, but the bundle's middle node has its edge rewritten after its SAIDs were computed, keeping the length, to name the presented ACDC instead of the root, with its top-level SAID left equal to the edge's n. Read by their claimed SAIDs the two nodes form a cycle. Recomputing the middle node's SAID (line 1174) shows it is not the node the edge names, so a validator that recomputes before it follows the node's own edges never meets the cycle and refuses the edge; one that indexes far nodes by their claimed SAID and walks first may never answer, which fails every assertion. The case's dag lists the edges of the nodes as issued, which hold no cycle. Its positive pair is KS-49 (ACDC-0059), which differs from it only in the defect.",
